:question
$()	<div style="font-family: verdana,  sans-serif ;  font-size: 11pt ; background-color: yellow ;">	<p> 	Let 
!insmath f
$() be the function defined over 
!insmath $val17
$() by: 
!insmath f(x) = $val30 
$().	</p><p> 	The aim of the exercise is to evaluate step by step the limit of  
!insmath f
$() at $val21 	 
!if $val20=1 
$()$val18 
!endif
$().	</p>	<small><b> 
!read oef/special.phtml help saisie,Typing hints 
$()</b></small>	</div>		<ul>			 
!if $m_step=1 
$()	<li>The function  
!insmath f
$() is of the form 
!insmath $val29
$() with:	<center>
!insmath u(x)
$() =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply1,5 
$() and  
!insmath k
$() =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply2,5 
$() </center>	</li>	 
!endif
$()	 
!if $m_step>1 
$()<li><font color = blue> The function  
!insmath f
$() is of the form  
!insmath $val29
$() with	
!insmath u(x) = $val23 
$() and 
!insmath k = $val8
$().</font> 	</li>	 
!endif
$()			 
!if $m_step=2 
$()	<li>Evaluate the limit of 
!insmath u
$() at $val21 : <small>( 
!read oef/special.phtml help saisie,typing hints 
$())</small>	<center>
!insmath \lim_{$val34} $val23 
$() =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply3,5 
$()</center>	</li>	 
!endif
$()	 
!if $m_step>2 
$()<li><font color = blue> The limit of 
!insmath u
$() at $val21  is</font>:  	<center>
!insmath \lim_{$val34} u(x) = \lim_{$val34} $val23  = $val33
$()</center>	</li>	 
!endif
$()		 
!if $m_step=3 
$()<li>Evaluate the limit of 
!insmath $val24
$() ar 
!insmath $val33
$(): <small>( 
!read oef/special.phtml help saisie,typing hints 
$())</small>	<center>
!insmath \lim_{$val35} $val24 
$() =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply4,5 
$()</center>	</li>	 
!endif
$()		 
!if $m_step>3 
$()<li><font color = blue>From the properties of the logarithm function, we know that</font>:  	<center>
!insmath \lim_{$val35} $val24   = $val41
$()</center>	</li>	 
!endif
$()			 
!if $m_step=4 
$()<li>By variable renaming 
!insmath t = u(x)
$() and by composition of limits, it comes that: <small>( 
!read oef/special.phtml help saisie,typing hints 
$())</small>	<center>
!insmath  \lim_{$val34} $val26   =  \lim_{$val34} $val27 
$() =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply5,5 
$()</center>	</li> 	 
!endif
$()		 
!if $m_step>4 
$()<li><font color = blue>By composition, the limit of 
!insmath $val25
$() at $val21 is</font>:	<center>	
!insmath \lim_{$val34} $val26  =  \lim_{$val34} $val27  = \lim_{$val35} $val24 = $val43
$().	</center> 	</li> 	 
!endif
$()		 
!if $m_step=5 
$()<li>Eventually, by the computational rules of the limits, it comes that: <small>( 
!read oef/special.phtml help saisie,Typing hints 
$())</small>	<center>
!insmath  \lim_{$val34} $val28
$()   =  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply6,5 
$()</center>	</li> 	 
!endif
$()		</ul>	
$()
!exit

